Package: [[name]]
# Not [[version]]: that is the Maven version, and apt compares on this line. Using it would
# make "dpkg -l | grep sokar-agent" report the Sokar release while the file name says which
# Claude Code it installs, and only the file name would be right.
Version: [[agent.cli.version]]-[[sokar.package.revision]]
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: fuin.org <info@fuin.org>
Homepage: https://github.com/fuinorg/sokar
Depends: sokar
Description: [[description]]
 Installs into /usr/libexec/sokar/agents, where the sokar binary looks for
 agents. Nothing needs to be registered: sokar scans that directory and asks
 whatever it finds to describe itself, so installing this package is enough.
 .
 This package is versioned as <agent-cli-version>-<sokar-release>, so
 "dpkg -l | grep sokar-agent" answers which agent CLI an image build will
 install without consulting the definition.
